<Base title="About" description="What DeskKaki is and how we research our home office guides."><article>
<h1>About DeskKaki</h1>
<p>"Kaki" is Singlish for a buddy. DeskKaki is meant to be the friend who has already done the homework on desks, chairs and gear before you spend your money.</p>
<p>A lot of home office advice online is written for American homes, American prices and American weather. We focus on what's actually sold in Singapore, at Singapore prices, for HDB-sized rooms and humid afternoons.</p>
<h2>How we research</h2>
<ul><li>We read manufacturer spec sheets and Singapore retailer listings directly, and note the date we checked prices.</li>
<li>We don't make up specs, prices or ratings. If we couldn't confirm a price on a real page, we leave it out and link you to the retailer.</li>
<li>Our guides are <strong>research-based roundups</strong>. Unless an article says otherwise, we have not physically tested the products.</li>
<li>We earn money through affiliate links. That never decides what we recommend; see our <a href={u('/affiliate-disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a>.</li></ul>
<p>Spotted an error or a price change? <a href={u('/contact/')}>Tell us</a> and we'll fix it.</p>
</article></Base>
